WEBVTT
NOTE Onboarding process workshop – 24 Sep 2026 – Teams recording transcript (excerpt)

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:31.000
<v Daniel Okafor>So the first thing that happens once the engagement manager's logged it, my team sends the document request. Usually same day, worst case next day.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:06:20.000
<v Daniel Okafor>Then we run the screening – sanctions, PEPs, adverse media – through the screening tool, and everything goes on the client file.

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:42.000
<v Sarah Lin>And the risk rating, is that still the matrix? Because I've seen people treat medium differently depending on who's doing it.

00:09:43.000 --> 00:10:05.000
<v Daniel Okafor>Yeah, it's the matrix for low and high. Medium is a bit of a judgement call, honestly.

00:14:32.000 --> 00:15:10.000
<v Priya Shah>One correction on the SOP – since the policy change in July, high-risk approval is done by me as MLRO, not the engagement partner. The partner is informed but they don't approve.

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:50.000
<v Daniel Okafor>The independence team then does the conflict check. If it's clear we accept, and the engagement manager sends the letter.

00:26:02.000 --> 00:26:40.000
<v Sarah Lin>What happens if the screening service is down? Last month we lost two days.

00:26:41.000 --> 00:26:55.000
<v Daniel Okafor>Good question. We just wait, I think. Nobody's written that down.
